1
00:00:00,290 --> 00:00:03,160
Why is a wind-turbine maker building

2
00:00:03,160 --> 00:00:04,420
an AI data centre?

3
00:00:04,650 --> 00:00:07,280
In Inner Mongolia, Envision is connecting

4
00:00:07,280 --> 00:00:09,040
those businesses through an AI campus

5
00:00:09,550 --> 00:00:10,680
called Galaxy.

6
00:00:10,890 --> 00:00:13,310
Follow the electricity to understand why

7
00:00:13,310 --> 00:00:15,510
an energy company wants to build

8
00:00:15,510 --> 00:00:15,880
it.

9
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:18,800
Envision founder and CEO Lei Zhang

10
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:21,520
started the company in 2007, making

11
00:00:21,520 --> 00:00:22,450
wind turbines.

12
00:00:22,450 --> 00:00:24,890
It expanded into batteries and energy

13
00:00:24,910 --> 00:00:25,800
systems.

14
00:00:26,010 --> 00:00:28,770
Computing creates demand for that equipment.

15
00:00:28,770 --> 00:00:31,820
Ulanqab sits about 300 kilometres northwest

16
00:00:31,820 --> 00:00:34,440
of Beijing, in China's Inner Mongolia.

17
00:00:34,640 --> 00:00:37,640
SemiAnalysis visited in September 2026.

18
00:00:37,640 --> 00:00:39,470
Its report is the starting point

19
00:00:39,470 --> 00:00:40,630
for this story.

20
00:00:40,850 --> 00:00:44,360
OpenAI's Stargate is the American comparison.

21
00:00:44,570 --> 00:00:47,160
Galaxy is a separate Envision project.

22
00:00:47,370 --> 00:00:50,610
SemiAnalysis reports 120 megawatts delivered in

23
00:00:50,610 --> 00:00:52,200
August, within a year.

24
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:54,570
Here, IT capacity means power intended

25
00:00:54,590 --> 00:00:57,400
for servers and other computing equipment.

26
00:00:57,400 --> 00:00:59,260
The report puts the full campus

27
00:00:59,260 --> 00:01:01,260
plan at 800 megawatts of IT

28
00:01:01,260 --> 00:01:02,170
capacity.

29
00:01:02,170 --> 00:01:03,790
A delivered phase and a future

30
00:01:03,790 --> 00:01:05,700
plan are different milestones.

31
00:01:05,700 --> 00:01:07,400
That distinction matters.

32
00:01:07,610 --> 00:01:09,410
Capacity alone cannot tell us how

33
00:01:09,410 --> 00:01:11,610
much useful AI computing is actually

34
00:01:11,610 --> 00:01:12,840
taking place.

35
00:01:13,090 --> 00:01:15,620
Accelerators process data, with memory and

36
00:01:15,620 --> 00:01:17,640
networks keeping them supplied.

37
00:01:17,850 --> 00:01:20,200
Power must reach those racks reliably.

38
00:01:20,410 --> 00:01:21,670
Their heat also has to leave

39
00:01:21,670 --> 00:01:22,760
the building.

40
00:01:22,940 --> 00:01:25,750
SemiAnalysis describes a five-megawatt pilot testing

41
00:01:25,750 --> 00:01:27,590
a different way of supplying the

42
00:01:27,590 --> 00:01:28,200
racks.

43
00:01:28,450 --> 00:01:32,000
Solid-state transformers convert incoming alternating current

44
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:34,890
into an 800-volt direct-current bus.

45
00:01:34,890 --> 00:01:36,800
At the same power, doubling DC

46
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:38,680
voltage halves the current in a

47
00:01:38,680 --> 00:01:39,610
conductor.

48
00:01:39,610 --> 00:01:41,790
At the same resistance, lower current

49
00:01:41,790 --> 00:01:43,410
reduces heating losses.

50
00:01:43,650 --> 00:01:46,080
Galaxy's actual savings need measuring.

51
00:01:46,080 --> 00:01:48,590
Rack electronics still reduce voltage further

52
00:01:48,590 --> 00:01:50,730
before that power reaches the chips.

53
00:01:50,730 --> 00:01:53,720
Envision also makes turbines and batteries,

54
00:01:53,720 --> 00:01:55,680
extending its role beyond owning the

55
00:01:55,680 --> 00:01:56,400
building.

56
00:01:56,400 --> 00:01:59,120
The company can coordinate generation, storage

57
00:01:59,120 --> 00:02:01,370
and equipment supplying power inside the

58
00:02:01,370 --> 00:02:02,000
campus.

59
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:03,920
But a wind farm's rated power

60
00:02:03,920 --> 00:02:05,590
is not its output at every

61
00:02:05,590 --> 00:02:06,400
moment.

62
00:02:06,690 --> 00:02:08,850
The wind rises and falls.

63
00:02:09,090 --> 00:02:11,770
Computing equipment needs reliable power through

64
00:02:11,770 --> 00:02:12,810
those changes.

65
00:02:12,810 --> 00:02:15,770
Batteries store some surplus electricity and

66
00:02:15,770 --> 00:02:18,300
supply it when generation falls below

67
00:02:18,300 --> 00:02:19,120
demand.

68
00:02:19,330 --> 00:02:22,370
Their usefulness depends on power, stored

69
00:02:22,370 --> 00:02:24,440
energy, and how long the calm

70
00:02:24,440 --> 00:02:25,280
lasts.

71
00:02:25,490 --> 00:02:27,980
'Wind-powered' does not establish that wind

72
00:02:27,980 --> 00:02:30,960
supplies all the electricity, every hour.

73
00:02:30,960 --> 00:02:32,820
How much of Galaxy is fitted

74
00:02:32,820 --> 00:02:35,360
with hardware and actually running remains

75
00:02:35,870 --> 00:02:36,880
unverified.

76
00:02:37,250 --> 00:02:39,430
Reported delivered capacity is not a

77
00:02:39,430 --> 00:02:41,870
measurement of load drawn by working

78
00:02:41,870 --> 00:02:42,800
servers.

79
00:02:43,010 --> 00:02:45,910
Buildings and megawatts cannot confirm installed

80
00:02:45,910 --> 00:02:47,850
chips, or how much work they

81
00:02:47,850 --> 00:02:48,640
produce.

82
00:02:48,810 --> 00:02:52,080
Envision's larger capacity announcements also need

83
00:02:52,080 --> 00:02:55,250
reconciling with SemiAnalysis's description of the

84
00:02:55,270 --> 00:02:56,080
campus.

85
00:02:56,290 --> 00:02:57,860
Those are questions for Zhang and

86
00:02:57,860 --> 00:03:00,420
the site's engineers, alongside the wider

87
00:03:00,910 --> 00:03:01,520
strategy.

88
00:03:01,520 --> 00:03:02,950
The next test is how much

89
00:03:03,040 --> 00:03:05,650
useful computing this energy system can

90
00:03:05,650 --> 00:03:06,320
deliver.
